{"text": "Watch the cloth before you read anything. This roll is a tan-mono, a bolt. In the old reckoning, one bolt is one kimono. Its width is settled before any tailor begins. In 1636, the shogunate went further and fixed by law how long and how wide a bolt of silk had to be. Keep that width in mind. Every measurement that follows is counted from it. Now the cut. There is no paper pattern and no outline of a body drawn on the cloth. The tailor only divides. Straight cuts across and along give eight pieces. Every strip has a place and nothing is thrown away. Then the pieces are joined again by hand. The stitches are kept small and out of sight on the face. Follow the seams. They run straight because every piece is straight. There is no dart and no curve. Hung on its rack, the robe is as flat as the bolt it came from, and yet it has to close around a person. Come round to the front and see how.", "duration": 65.44, "timestamps": {"word": [{"word": "Watch", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.38}, {"word": "the", "start": 0.44, "end": 0.52}, {"word": "cloth", "start": 0.58, "end": 0.92}, {"word": "before", "start": 1, "end": 1.24}, {"word": "you", "start": 1.3, "end": 1.44}, {"word": "read", "start": 1.52, "end": 1.76}, {"word": "anything.", "start": 1.84, "end": 2.28}, {"word": "This", "start": 2.82, "end": 3}, {"word": "roll", "start": 3.06, "end": 3.38}, {"word": "is", "start": 3.44, "end": 3.52}, {"word": "a", "start": 3.58, "end": 3.64}, {"word": "tan-mono,", "start": 3.7, "end": 4.44}, {"word": "a", "start": 4.8, "end": 4.84}, {"word": "bolt.", "start": 4.96, "end": 5.34}, {"word": "In", "start": 5.92, "end": 5.98}, {"word": "the", "start": 6.02, "end": 6.1}, {"word": "old", "start": 6.16, "end": 6.32}, {"word": "reckoning,", "start": 6.38, "end": 6.78}, {"word": "one", "start": 7.04, "end": 7.18}, {"word": "bolt", "start": 7.26, "end": 7.46}, {"word": "is", "start": 7.54, "end": 7.68}, {"word": "one", "start": 7.78, "end": 7.96}, {"word": "kimono.", "start": 8.02, "end": 